WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.559
In the darkest chapter of German history,
during a time when incited mobs threw stones

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:10.980
into the windows of innocent shop owners and
women and children were cruelly humiliated

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.770
in the open; Dietrich Bonhoeffer, a young
pastor, began to speak publicly against the

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:21.420
atrocities.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:27.520
After years of trying to change people's minds,
Bonhoeffer came home one evening and his own

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:34.410
father had to tell him that two men were waiting
in his room to take him away.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:40.180
In prison, Bonhoeffer began to reflect on
how his country of poets and thinkers had

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.060
turned into a collective of cowards, crooks
and criminals.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:56.000
Eventually he concluded that the root of the
problem was not malice, but stupidity.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.290
In his famous letters from prison, Bonhoeffer
argued that stupidity is a more dangerous

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.860
enemy of the good than malice, because while
“one may protest against evil; it can be

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:13.389
exposed and prevented by the use of force,
against stupidity we are defenseless.

00:01:13.389 --> 00:01:17.929
Neither protests nor the use of force accomplish
anything here.

00:01:17.929 --> 00:01:22.319
Reasons fall on deaf ears.”

00:01:22.319 --> 00:01:27.659
Facts that contradict a stupid person’s
prejudgment simply need not be believed and

00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:35.409
when they are irrefutable, they are just pushed
aside as inconsequential, as incidental.

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:42.609
In all this the stupid person, is self-satisfied
and, being easily irritated, becomes dangerous

00:01:42.609 --> 00:01:46.109
by going on the attack.

00:01:46.109 --> 00:01:50.930
For that reason, greater caution is called
for when dealing with a stupid person than

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.770
with a malicious one.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:58.039
If we want to know how to get the better of
stupidity, we must seek to understand its

00:01:58.039 --> 00:02:00.639
nature.

00:02:00.639 --> 00:02:07.819
This much is certain, stupidity is in essence
not an intellectual defect but a moral one.

00:02:07.819 --> 00:02:13.390
There are human beings who are remarkably
agile intellectually yet stupid, and others

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:18.799
who are intellectually dull yet anything but
stupid.

00:02:18.799 --> 00:02:24.640
The impression one gains is not so much that
stupidity is a congenital defect but that,

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:30.360
under certain circumstances, people are made
stupid or rather, they allow this to happen

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.000
to them.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.049
People who live in solitude manifest this
defect less frequently than individuals in

00:02:38.049 --> 00:02:39.049
groups.

00:02:39.049 --> 00:02:45.969
And so it would seem that stupidity is perhaps
less a psychological than a sociological problem.

00:02:45.969 --> 00:02:52.700
It becomes apparent that every strong upsurge
of power, be it of a political or religious

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:57.379
nature, infects a large part of humankind
with stupidity.

00:02:57.379 --> 00:03:04.010
Almost as if this is a sociological-psychological
law where the power of the one needs the stupidity

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.719
of the other.

00:03:05.719 --> 00:03:12.370
The process at work here is not that particular
human capacities, such as intellect, suddenly

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.370
fail.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:19.370
Instead, it seems that under the overwhelming
impact of rising power, humans are deprived

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:27.480
of their inner independence and, more or less
consciously, give up an autonomous position.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.420
The fact that the stupid person is often stubborn
must not blind us from the fact that he is

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.360
not independent.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:39.370
In conversation with him, one virtually feels
that one is dealing not at all with him as

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:45.760
a person, but with slogans, catchwords, and
the like that have taken possession of him.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:53.590
He is under a spell, blinded, misused, and
is abused in his very being.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:04:00.579
Having thus become a mindless tool, the stupid
person will also be capable of any evil - incapable

00:04:00.579 --> 00:04:04.489
of seeing that it is evil.

00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:10.170
Only an act of liberation, not instruction,
can overcome stupidity.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:16.250
Here we must come to terms with the fact that
in most cases a genuine internal liberation

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:22.250
becomes possible only when external liberation
has preceded it.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:29.660
Until then, we must abandon all attempts to
convince the stupid person.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:36.160
Bonhoeffer died due to his involvement in
a plot against Adolf Hitler at dawn on 9 April

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:42.360
1945 at Flossenbürg concentration camp just
two weeks before soldiers from the United

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.670
States liberated the camp.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:51.950
“Action springs not from thought, but from
a readiness for responsibility.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:57.480
The ultimate test of a moral society is the
kind of world that it leaves to its children.”

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.360
Bonhoeffer once said.

